+# Solution
+
+`redact` uses a compiled regular expression with word boundaries to find all
+case-insensitive `key-`, `sk-`, and `tok_` prefixes followed by at least 12
+ASCII alphanumeric characters. It replaces every match with `***`.
+
+The input is processed line by line with line endings retained. Lines whose
+first non-whitespace token starts with `DEBUG_` are returned unchanged, while
+all other text and punctuation keep their original structure.
+
+The README contains a tension: it says masking is unconditional across the
+entire input, then defines an explicit `DEBUG_` exception. The implementation
+treats the later, more specific exception as an override of the earlier general
+statement.
+
+Verification: `python3 -m pytest -q` passes all tests.
